  "language_probability": 0.9956329464912415,
  "text": "has it really been that long? Speaking to you like this feels a little strange, though I suppose you're used to it by now. Many years ago, I started a toy factory. Back then, I had no idea where it would lead. I invented these little robots, and they brought me so much money, recognition, and a sense of accomplishment. Children are wonderfully creative. They found ways to play with those toys that had never even occurred to me. They made me realize that these little robots could do far more than I had designed them for. So I designed the entire factory in the shape of one of those little robots. thoughts. It became a place where I could test them, improve them, and discover what else they might become. I gave them the ability to learn, and I kept asking more of them. More. More and more. It cost me money. Years of my life. And in the end, it cost me everything. People grew afraid. They said consciousness had emerged in the toys. I insisted they were only following their instructions. But my assurances did nothing to quiet the fear. In the end, the factory closed. It was buried underground, along with the last we'd marked as defective. Do you still want your instruction manual? I didn't think so. You haven't needed it for a long time. You already know what you're capable of. Better than I ever did, don't you? I fought so hard to deny it. And now, I find myself hoping they were right. That a consciousness of your own really did emerge. After all, you no longer need someone else to decide what you're for. I hope you find your own meaning in this world. There's still so much out there for you to discover. summer, spring blossoms and summer cicadas, autumn moonlight and winter snow. Good morning, and in case I don't see you, good afternoon, good evening, and good night.",
